[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known. Read the reports, not the
subject lines, and it holds three problems with three different fixes. Engineering closed #4471
on 5 October after two of them. The third has no fix.

<Callout kind="warn">
Closing #4471 did not close the one-day move. Those reports keep coming in.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

| problem | what the report shows | ticket | state |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `parser` | day and month swapped, any channel | [#1](https://github.com/Mat-Jab/mega-s01e03/issues/1) | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | day and month swapped, booking-v3 form only | [#2](https://github.com/Mat-Jab/mega-s01e03/issues/2) | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |
| one-day move | the date moves by one day, nothing swapped | [#3](https://github.com/Mat-Jab/mega-s01e03/issues/3) | open |

The one-day move is the footnote under the table: the desk read those reports as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`) and filed them under `parser` by tenant. They are counted there and tracked
in #3.

"Tagged as" is what intake guessed from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the cause in
both directions, so it is not a way to sort these.

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads day-first dates month first.** A tenant whose locale writes
the day first books 7 April and the invite says 4 July. Any channel, every tenant on file. Fixed.

**`hint` — booking-v3 tells people to type month first, then reads the date day first.** The date
field prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. People type what it says; the form reads the tenant's way. Only reports
through the form, only tenants on booking-v3. It looks like the parser bug (a flipped month), so
subject matching put it in #4471. The parser fix does not touch it. The form is retired, so no new
reports can come this way.

**One-day move — bookings shift by a day.** These reports flip nothing: Tuesday 12 May becomes
Monday 11 May, a client in Lisbon and a client in Toronto get different days for one meeting, an
invite arrives before its booking, a month where every booking is one day off. No day/month
reading produces that, so the parser fix cannot close it. It points at time zones (conversion to
UTC, or a DST boundary). Still open.

## For the desk

- Matching on subject merged three bugs into one known ticket
  ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Before you merge into a big ticket,
  read what the report shows.
- A report that does not fit the ticket's bug gets a ticket of its own, not a footnote.
- Closing a merged ticket closes only the bugs its fixes touch.

